    "theorem": "For every conference matrix of order n=p\u00b2+1 (p odd prime): rows r_i of an ONB of V\u208a satisfy \u2016r_i\u2016\u00b2=1/2, r_i\u00b7r_j=C_ij/(2p); G_ij=(r_i\u00b7r_j)\u00b2 = a I + b 11^T with a=(p\u00b2\u22121)/(4p\u00b2)>0, a+nb=1/2, so rank G=n. Hence {r_i r_i^T} are lin. independent, the diagonal map Sym\u2192R^n is surjective, and on Sym_0 its image is 1^\u22a5 (rank n\u22121). Therefore dim Z = d(d+1)/2 \u2212 1 \u2212 (n\u22121) = d(d\u22123)/2.",
